<statement>
<p>
Solve the following linear system.  If the system has an infinite number of solutions, parameterize the solution set in terms of the free variables of the original system.</p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{\left\lbrace\begin{array}{ccccccccc} -{3}{x}\amp+\amp{21}{y}\amp+\amp{5}{z}\amp-\amp{28}{w}\amp=\amp{6}\\{2}{x}\amp-\amp{14}{y}\amp-\amp{z}\amp+\amp{14}{w}\amp=\amp-{11}\\-{2}{x}\amp+\amp{14}{y}\amp+\amp{8}{z}\amp-\amp{28}{w}\amp=\amp-{10}\end{array}\right.}</m></p>
<p>
x = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
y = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
z = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
w = <fillin characters="20"/>  

</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li><m>\displaystyle-{7}+{7}{y}-{6}{w}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{y}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle-{3}+{2}{w}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{w}</m></li></ul></p>
</answer>

